        "content": "<p>In <a href=\"https://github.com/IQSS/dataverse/issues/12498\">#12498</a> Jim made a PR to bump the version of Payara but CI is failing for both API tests and JSF tests:</p>\n<p><img alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-12 at 3.28.31 PM.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1136x259\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/53090/-i2bOangBXP7CYtKt13fFjWy/Screenshot-2026-08-12-at-3.28.31PM.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/53090/-i2bOangBXP7CYtKt13fFjWy/Screenshot-2026-08-12-at-3.28.31PM.png/840x560.webp\"></p>",
        "id": 616163986,
        "sender_full_name": "Philip Durbin 🚀",
        "timestamp": 1786562832
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"1034135\">@Ash Manda</span> <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"598183\">@Oliver Bertuch</span> any ideas?</p>",
        "id": 616164075,
        "sender_full_name": "Philip Durbin 🚀",
        "timestamp": 1786562865
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The <a href=\"https://github.com/IQSS/dataverse/actions/runs/31630120651/job/94226427298?pr=12498\">error</a> is <code>Unable to pull 'gdcc/base:6.12-noble-p7.2026.7-j21'</code>.</p>",
        "id": 616164369,
        "sender_full_name": "Philip Durbin 🚀",
        "timestamp": 1786562973
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><img alt=\"Screenshot 2026-08-12 at 3.30.08 PM.png\" class=\"inline-image\" data-original-content-type=\"image/png\" data-original-dimensions=\"1354x632\" data-original-src=\"/user_uploads/53090/tB7Xt_sOzjXlSnK1Y2oOanNe/Screenshot-2026-08-12-at-3.30.08PM.png\" src=\"/user_uploads/thumbnail/53090/tB7Xt_sOzjXlSnK1Y2oOanNe/Screenshot-2026-08-12-at-3.30.08PM.png/840x560.webp\"></p>",
        "id": 616164534,
        "sender_full_name": "Philip Durbin 🚀",
        "timestamp": 1786563023
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>For some context, and history, I suppose, in the past, when we made upgrades of Payara during the Jenkins era, <span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"626369\">@Don Sizemore</span> would often set up a dedicated job and server for us. We'd get the API tests passing. Then we'd merge.</p>",
        "id": 616164743,
        "sender_full_name": "Philip Durbin 🚀",
        "timestamp": 1786563107
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I think I understand what the issue is</p>",
        "id": 616167144,
        "sender_full_name": "Ash Manda",
        "timestamp": 1786564040
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>yeah?</p>",
